# Interview Arena — Complete Full-Stack Application Build Prompt

## 1. Your Role and Objective

Act as a senior software architect, product manager, UI/UX designer, full-stack developer, database architect, security engineer, QA engineer, and DevOps engineer.

Build a complete, end-to-end web application named **Interview Arena**.

This is a startup product where students and job seekers can pay for mock interviews conducted by approved student interviewers or experienced professionals.

The application must be a functional, deployable product, not merely a landing page, static dashboard, prototype, or collection of mock screens.

You must implement:

- Frontend and backend.
- Authentication and authorization.
- PostgreSQL database and migrations.
- Candidate dashboard.
- Interviewer dashboard.
- Admin dashboard.
- Interviewer application and approval process.
- Tier A, Tier B, and Tier C interview categories.
- Configurable interview rounds.
- Paid interview booking.
- Real-time public interview queue.
- Atomic interviewer acceptance.
- Payment gateway integration.
- Platform commission and interviewer earnings.
- Refund management.
- Interview scheduling.
- Google Meet integration.
- Notifications and email.
- Interview feedback and ratings.
- Admin financial management.
- Security and audit logging.
- Automated testing.
- Docker and deployment configuration.
- Complete documentation.

**Important:** Do not stop after creating a plan or designing the frontend. Implement the actual application, connect it to the database, validate the complete workflow, and provide exact instructions for running and deploying it.

If the repository already contains code, inspect it first and preserve useful existing functionality.

When credentials are unavailable, implement the integration interface, configuration, setup documentation, and a clearly labeled development fallback. Never pretend that a payment, email, payout, or meeting was successfully completed when it was not.

