# 2. Product Overview

## Product name

Interview Arena

## Target audience

- College students.
- Freshers.
- Software engineers.
- Job seekers.
- Candidates preparing for product-based companies.
- Candidates preparing for service-based companies.
- Experienced professionals changing jobs.
- People preparing for technical, behavioral, and system design interviews.

## Core concept

The platform has three interview categories:

- Tier A: highly competitive company preparation.
- Tier B: established companies and moderately competitive interviews.
- Tier C: entry-level, smaller-company, and fundamentals-focused interviews.

Candidates select a company preparation track, choose an interview round, pay the applicable price, and join a queue.

Approved interviewers can see eligible waiting sessions and accept them.

Once an interviewer accepts a session, the system must assign that session to exactly one interviewer, notify both participants, and provide a real meeting link through the configured meeting provider.

After the interview, the interviewer submits feedback and earns the configured share of the session fee.

The platform retains its configured commission.

The application must clearly state that these are simulated practice interviews and that company preparation tracks do not imply official partnerships or guarantee employment.

