# 11. Real-Time Queue and Concurrency

The queue is a core feature and must be implemented correctly.

Use WebSockets, SSE, or another suitable real-time technology. A polling fallback is acceptable if documented.

Requirements:

- Separate queues by compatible tier, role, track, round, language, and skills.
- Default to FIFO ordering.
- Make any prioritization rules configurable and explainable.
- Show only eligible requests to each interviewer.
- Prevent duplicate queue entries.
- Prevent duplicate payment fulfillment.
- Prevent overlapping interviewer assignments.
- Support cancellation.
- Support interviewer claim expiration.
- Recover abandoned assignments.
- Handle browser refresh and network disconnects.
- Provide a reliable queue state after reconnecting.
- Notify participants when assignment changes.
- Record booking and queue events for auditing.

Use PostgreSQL transactions, row-level locks, conditional updates, or an equivalent atomic mechanism.

For example, if two interviewers accept the same booking simultaneously, only one transaction may succeed. The other must receive a clear message that the session has already been claimed.

